  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 is far weaker at 0.208, indicating RNA is the dominant signal source. With only two experiments completed, the most important unresolved question is whether moving from single to multiprofile improves the RNA baseline. This experiment (config_002) isolates that single variable—multiprofile with avgpool aggregation—while keeping the proven PCA n2000 encoder and RNA-only setting constant. It is the most informative next step because: (1) it directly extends our best-performing configuration with a minimal, interpretable change; (2) if multiprofile helps, it validates a key architectural axis and justifies further investment in multiprofile variants (transformer, different encoders); if it does not help, it tells us single profile is sufficient and redirects budget toward encoder choice or multimodal fusion; (3) avgpool is the simpler aggregation, making it a cleaner first test before the more complex transformer. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

